WEBVTT

00:00:07.257 --> 00:00:10.051
( fast-tempo, eerie melody
playing )

00:00:17.851 --> 00:00:21.104
( river gurgling )

00:00:28.069 --> 00:00:30.238
♪ ♪

00:00:38.538 --> 00:00:43.710
( eerie melody transitions
into light, wondrous theme )

00:00:43.793 --> 00:00:45.003
Stop the boat.

00:00:45.045 --> 00:00:47.213
I want to show you guys
something.

00:00:51.551 --> 00:00:53.887
( whirring and clinking )

00:00:53.970 --> 00:00:57.265
( steam hissing )

00:01:07.025 --> 00:01:11.071
Now, this is the most important
room in the entire factory.

00:01:11.112 --> 00:01:12.280
Now, everyone

00:01:12.364 --> 00:01:15.116
enjoy yourselves,
but just don’t touch anything.

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:16.368
Okay?

00:01:16.409 --> 00:01:17.160
Go on!

00:01:17.243 --> 00:01:18.787
Go on, scoot! Scoot!

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:22.916
( burbling )

00:01:29.673 --> 00:01:32.050
Hey, Mr. Wonka, what’s this?

00:01:32.092 --> 00:01:33.802
Oh!

00:01:33.885 --> 00:01:36.262
Let me show you.

00:01:37.430 --> 00:01:38.598
Thank you.

00:01:38.640 --> 00:01:40.850
These are Everlasting
Gobstoppers.

00:01:40.934 --> 00:01:42.102
They’re for children

00:01:42.143 --> 00:01:43.770
who are given very little
allowance money.

00:01:43.812 --> 00:01:46.564
You can suck on it all year,
and it’ll never get any smaller.

00:01:46.606 --> 00:01:47.774
( giggles )

00:01:47.816 --> 00:01:48.900
Isn’t that neat?

00:01:48.942 --> 00:01:50.610
It’s like gum.

00:01:50.652 --> 00:01:51.945
No.

00:01:51.986 --> 00:01:53.363
Gum is for chewing.

00:01:53.446 --> 00:01:55.824
And if you tried chewing
one of these gobstoppers,

00:01:55.907 --> 00:01:57.367
you’d break all
your little teeth off.

00:01:57.450 --> 00:01:59.202
They sure do taste

00:01:59.285 --> 00:02:01.371
terrific.

00:02:06.459 --> 00:02:07.585
( steam hissing )

00:02:07.627 --> 00:02:09.796
And this is hair toffee.

00:02:09.838 --> 00:02:12.674
You suck down one
of these little boogers,

00:02:12.757 --> 00:02:14.676
and in exactly half an hour,

00:02:14.759 --> 00:02:16.761
a brand-new crop of hair
will start growing out

00:02:16.803 --> 00:02:18.638
all over the top
of your little noggin.

00:02:18.680 --> 00:02:20.056
And a mustache.

00:02:20.140 --> 00:02:21.599
And a beard.

00:02:21.641 --> 00:02:22.684
Who wants a beard?

00:02:22.767 --> 00:02:25.520
Well, beatniks for one.

00:02:25.603 --> 00:02:27.439
Folk singers
and motorbike riders.

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:28.648
You know...

00:02:28.690 --> 00:02:30.400
all those hip, jazzy,
super-cool, neat,

00:02:30.483 --> 00:02:31.651
keen and
groovy cats.

00:02:31.693 --> 00:02:32.819
It’s in the fridge,
daddy-o.

00:02:32.861 --> 00:02:34.154
Are you hep to the jive?

00:02:34.195 --> 00:02:35.613
Can you dig
what I’m laying down?

00:02:35.655 --> 00:02:36.823
I knew that you could.
Slide me

00:02:36.865 --> 00:02:37.741
some skin,

00:02:37.824 --> 00:02:39.993
soul brother.

00:02:42.412 --> 00:02:44.748
Unfortunately, the mixture
isn’t quite right yet,

00:02:44.831 --> 00:02:46.082
’cause an Oompa-Loompa
tried some

00:02:46.166 --> 00:02:48.334
yesterday, and well, he...

00:02:52.505 --> 00:02:54.340
How are you today?

00:02:56.259 --> 00:02:57.802
You look great.

00:03:05.894 --> 00:03:07.687
Watch this.

00:03:07.771 --> 00:03:08.855
( alarm blares )

00:03:08.938 --> 00:03:11.024
( steam hissing )

00:03:11.065 --> 00:03:12.358
( mechanical whirring )

00:03:12.442 --> 00:03:14.194
( steam hissing )

00:03:18.198 --> 00:03:22.535
( whirring increases
in speed and volume )

00:03:23.787 --> 00:03:26.498
( bubbling )

00:03:32.962 --> 00:03:35.882
( bell dings )

00:03:35.965 --> 00:03:37.509
You mean that’s it?

00:03:37.550 --> 00:03:39.886
Do you even know
what "it" is?

00:03:39.969 --> 00:03:41.262
It’s gum.

00:03:41.346 --> 00:03:42.222
Yeah.

00:03:42.305 --> 00:03:43.473
It’s a stick
of the most amazing

00:03:43.556 --> 00:03:45.642
and sensational gum
in the whole universe.

00:03:45.725 --> 00:03:47.352
Know why?

00:03:47.393 --> 00:03:48.645
Know why?

00:03:48.728 --> 00:03:49.854
’Cause this gum is a full

00:03:49.896 --> 00:03:51.606
three-course dinner
all by itself.

00:03:51.689 --> 00:03:53.066
( giggles )

00:03:54.818 --> 00:03:56.820
Why would anyone want that?

00:03:56.903 --> 00:03:59.906
Uh... uh...

00:04:03.451 --> 00:04:05.537
"It will be the end
of all kitchens

00:04:05.578 --> 00:04:06.663
"and all cooking.

00:04:06.746 --> 00:04:07.956
"Just a little
strip of Wonka’s

00:04:08.039 --> 00:04:09.332
"magic chewing
gum, and that is

00:04:09.415 --> 00:04:10.375
"all you will...

00:04:10.416 --> 00:04:12.126
ever need at breakfast,
lunch and dinner."

00:04:12.210 --> 00:04:13.837
This piece of
gum happens

00:04:13.920 --> 00:04:17.590
to be tomato soup,
roast beef and blueberry pie.

00:04:17.632 --> 00:04:19.634
It sounds great.

00:04:19.717 --> 00:04:21.636
It sounds weird.

00:04:21.719 --> 00:04:23.263
It sounds like
my kind of gum.

00:04:25.765 --> 00:04:27.100
I-I’d rather you didn’t.

00:04:27.183 --> 00:04:29.185
There are still one
or two things that are little...

00:04:29.269 --> 00:04:31.145
I’m the world record-holder
in chewing gum.

00:04:31.229 --> 00:04:32.605
I’m not afraid
of anything.

00:04:37.986 --> 00:04:39.571
How is it, honey?

00:04:39.612 --> 00:04:40.905
It’s amazing!

00:04:40.947 --> 00:04:42.073
Tomato soup!

00:04:42.115 --> 00:04:43.950
I can feel it
running down my throat!

00:04:44.033 --> 00:04:45.493
Yeah. Spit it out.

00:04:45.577 --> 00:04:47.078
Young lady, I think
you’d better...

00:04:47.120 --> 00:04:48.204
It’s changing.

00:04:48.288 --> 00:04:51.457
Roast beef with baked potato.

00:04:51.541 --> 00:04:53.042
Crispy skin and butter.

00:04:53.126 --> 00:04:54.460
Keep chewing, kiddo.

00:04:54.544 --> 00:04:56.129
My little girl’s gonna be
the first person in the

00:04:56.212 --> 00:04:57.463
world to have
a chewing gum meal.

00:04:57.505 --> 00:04:58.506
WONKA:
Yeah.

00:04:58.590 --> 00:05:00.550
I’m just a little concerned
about the...

00:05:00.633 --> 00:05:02.468
Blueberry pie and ice cream.

00:05:02.552 --> 00:05:03.803
That part.

00:05:03.845 --> 00:05:05.638
What’s happening to her nose?

00:05:10.852 --> 00:05:12.478
It’s turning blue.

00:05:13.897 --> 00:05:15.023
MRS. BEAUREGARDE:
Your whole

00:05:15.106 --> 00:05:16.941
nose has gone purple.

00:05:16.983 --> 00:05:19.527
What do you mean?

00:05:19.611 --> 00:05:20.695
MRS. BEAUREGARDE:
Voilet,

00:05:20.778 --> 00:05:21.988
you’re turning violet.

00:05:23.031 --> 00:05:24.657
What’s happening?!

00:05:24.699 --> 00:05:25.783
Well, I told you

00:05:25.825 --> 00:05:27.201
I hadn’t quite got it right,

00:05:27.285 --> 00:05:28.411
’cause it goes a little

00:05:28.494 --> 00:05:30.580
funny when it gets
to the dessert.

00:05:30.663 --> 00:05:32.665
It’s the blueberry
pie that does it.

00:05:32.749 --> 00:05:35.084
I’m terribly sorry.

00:05:35.168 --> 00:05:36.669
( grunts )

00:05:43.384 --> 00:05:47.597
Mother, what’s
happening to me?

00:05:51.601 --> 00:05:52.685
( groans )

00:05:53.895 --> 00:05:57.523
( burbling )

00:05:57.565 --> 00:05:59.859
Oh. Oh! Oh!

00:05:59.943 --> 00:06:02.028
She’s swelling up.

00:06:05.698 --> 00:06:07.075
Like a blueberry.

00:06:07.158 --> 00:06:09.994
( groaning )

00:06:15.208 --> 00:06:17.502
( groaning )

